1
00:00:00,149 --> 00:00:02,249
(Sheldon:)Fine.

2
00:00:02,251 --> 00:00:04,481
LEONARD:
Yeah, okay, I see him.

3
00:00:04,487 --> 00:00:06,087
(Leonard:)It looks like
they're having a nice time.

4
00:00:06,088 --> 00:00:07,388
(Leonard:)I wish I could hear
what they're saying.

5
00:00:07,390 --> 00:00:08,660
(Bernadette:)Yeah, I should've brought

6
00:00:08,658 --> 00:00:09,828
(Bernadette:)my parabolic microphone.

7
00:00:09,825 --> 00:00:11,895
(Penny:)Your what?
Nothing. Not important.

8
00:00:13,328 --> 00:00:14,758
(Dave:)So you've never
been married?

9
00:00:14,764 --> 00:00:17,894
(Amy:)No. I mean,
to be completely honest, I've...

10
00:00:17,900 --> 00:00:20,270
(Amy:)I've only been
in one long-term relationship.

11
00:00:20,269 --> 00:00:21,599
(Dave:)Oh. What happened with that?

12
00:00:21,604 --> 00:00:23,174
(Amy:)That's a good question.

13
00:00:28,090 --> 00:00:29,360
(Amy:)After five years,

14
00:00:29,359 --> 00:00:32,089
(Amy:)it was just feeling like
more work than it should be.

15
00:00:32,095 --> 00:00:33,225
(Dave:)Oh, that's too bad.

16
00:00:33,229 --> 00:00:34,829
(Dave:)Was he a neurobiologist
like you?

17
00:00:34,831 --> 00:00:37,161
(Amy:)No. He's a theoretical physicist

18
00:00:37,167 --> 00:00:40,097
(Amy:)at Caltech.

19
00:00:40,103 --> 00:00:43,033
(Dave:)I love teaching math, but
that would be my dream job.

20
00:00:43,039 --> 00:00:44,309
(Dave:)What's his focus?

21
00:00:44,307 --> 00:00:47,647
(Amy:)Um... used to be string theory,
now it's dark matter.

22
00:00:47,644 --> 00:00:49,714
(Amy:)But... let's
not discuss Sheldon.

23
00:00:49,712 --> 00:00:51,612
(Amy:)Let's get back to you.

24
00:00:51,614 --> 00:00:55,084
(Dave:)Wait, you're not talking
about Dr. Sheldon Cooper?

25
00:00:56,351 --> 00:01:00,021
(Amy:)I'm trying not to.

